    "remedies_unknowns": {
      "exposure": "Supreme Court allowed passport-marker restrictions in November 2025 and upheld an analogous minor-care ban quoted by the division high court in January 2026. Passport, executive-order and health-rule challenges remain unresolved, so present exposure depends on which measures are operative.",
      "protection": "Civil-liberties litigation, other injunctions/blocks, legal-aid passport guidance, federal hate-crime law and division hate-crime coverage show courts and remedies are not wholly unavailable, reducing severity below a no-recourse regime.",
      "interaction": "Remedies are strongest against some national executive orders and weakest where the highest courts have now allowed the operative passport and care regimes; that interaction leaves entry and minor-care risks largely unremedied.",
