  "synthesis": "The traveller encounters one interacting system, not separable national and division layers. Document discrepancy can trigger visa refusal or a possible lifetime fraud bar; entry/facility checks can trigger criminal trespass and birth-sex placement; detention can trigger care removal and documented abuse; for a minor, care, school and sports rules transfer risk to providers and guardians. Courts, injunctions, hate-crime coverage and grandfathering prevent the lowest tier, but the highest courts have allowed the central passport and analogous care regimes, and many punitive provisions compound rather than cancel. Hence an Elevated-Risk score around 0.40."
